This is more or less what I've been talking about.
5.1-RELEASE-alpha-miniinst.iso is 236M, which is way too big.

If you take a 4.x boot.flp, you should also be able to dd that onto a
SCSI disk and boot it.  So what we need is an image that conatains only a
minimal memory filesystem /, a full GENERIC kernel, and full set of
modules.  This image will come in under 8MB.
 
